<title>UK: UK M4 grows provisional s/a 9.8 pct in year to Jan.</title>
<headline>UK M4 grows provisional s/a 9.8 pct in year to Jan.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of England published the following data on UK monetary aggregates for January -</p>
<p>    MONEY SUPPLY				     Jan	 Dec *</p>
<p>    M4 in month	  (adjusted)		9.8	-0.3</p>
<p>	  in year to date (adjusted)	     1.6	 9.5</p>
<p>    M4 in month	  (unadjusted)	    0.6	-0.1</p>
<p>	  in year to date (unadjusted)	   9.9	 9.4</p>
<p>Adjusted lending by banks, building</p>
<p>     societies in billions of stg	     12.8	 n/a</p>
<p>NOTE - consensus forecasts M4 9.1 pct yr/yr, M4 lending +7.2 billion stg. * Previously published final figures for Dec</p>
<p>-- LONDON NEWSROOM ++44 171 542 7708</p>
</text>
